\begin{cases} a_1 + 2d = 17 \\ a_1 + 4d = 39 \end{cases}
\] Subtracting the first equation from the second gives \(2d = 22\), so \(d = 11\). Substituting \(d = 11\) into the first equation gives \(a_1 + 2(11) = 17\), so \(a_1 = 17 - 22 = -5\). Now we can find the 7th term: \(a_7 = a_1 + 6d = -5 + 6(11) = -5 + 66 = 61\). </think> <answer> 61 </answer>

